---Contains the current state and details of the requested issue.
---@class aws.continuum.GetCodeIssueOutput
---@field issueId aws.continuum.IssueId The unique identifier of the issue.
---@field issueArn aws.continuum.IssueArn The ARN of the issue.
---@field name aws.continuum.IssueName The name of the issue.
---@field synopsis aws.continuum.IssueSynopsis A free-form synopsis of the issue.
---@field severity? aws.continuum.IssueSeverity Current severity: the FindingSeverity seed at create, overwritten by the authoritative severity that prioritization assigns after validation.
---@field confidence? aws.continuum.IssueConfidence The likelihood that this issue is a true positive, expressed as a percentage (0-100).
---@field severityReasoning? aws.continuum.IssueSeverityReasoning The justification for the current severity. Always leads with a customer-facing basis clause synthesized from how the severity was determined (e.g. "Severity from finding.", "Severity from Continuum system."); when prioritization has run, its own reasoning follows. Issues created before the basis clause was introduced return their original reasoning without it.
---@field summary? aws.continuum.IssueRemediationSummary The remediation completion summary, when the green stage has run.
---@field findingIds aws.continuum.IssueFindingIds The findings that motivated this issue. Bare identifiers only -- a caller authorized for GetCodeIssue is not necessarily authorized to read finding detail; call GetCodeFinding for that. Every referenced finding is included regardless of origin (both CustomerUploaded and ContinuumScanner).
---@field status aws.continuum.IssueStatus The current lifecycle status of the issue.
---@field phase? aws.continuum.IssuePhase The part of the workflow the issue is in. Present when status is IN_PROGRESS, and when status is FAILED and the failing phase is known.
---@field statusReason? aws.continuum.IssueStatusReason Why the issue failed. Present only when status is FAILED.
---@field statusMessage? aws.continuum.IssueStatusMessage Customer-facing explanation of statusReason. Present only when status is FAILED.
