---Projected content for a PATCH artifact: the remediation patch for one repository, with the descriptors needed to verify and apply it and the state of its delivery to the customer's own bucket or repository.
---@class aws.continuum.PatchBody
---@field patch aws.continuum.IssueArtifactContent The patch exactly as stored, unmodified. Control Plane accepted it only as a text unified diff, so `git apply` applies it.
---@field format? aws.continuum.PatchFormat The patch's wire format, read from the patch itself, which determines how to apply it. Absent when the patch starts with neither a git mailbox header nor a `diff --git` header.
---@field repositoryName? aws.continuum.BuildRepositoryName The repository the patch applies to, as named in the source snapshot it was generated against.
---@field patchSha256 aws.continuum.ArtifactSha256 SHA-256 of the patch's UTF-8 bytes in lowercase hex, computed by Control Plane when it stored the patch. Lets a caller confirm the patch it applies is byte-for-byte the one that was reviewed. Computed over the patch bytes, so it is verifiable against `patch` without trusting this value.
---@field sizeBytes number Size of the patch in UTF-8 bytes, the unit the digest is computed over.
---@field delivery? aws.continuum.PatchDelivery Delivery of the patch to the customer's bucket or repository. Absent when the artifact has no delivery destination.

---Policy governing whether Continuum creates a patch for a proposed remediation.
---@alias aws.continuum.PatchCreationPolicy "ENABLED"|"DISABLED"

---Delivery of a patch to a destination the customer owns: an object in the environment's source bucket or a pull request in the source repository.
---@class aws.continuum.PatchDelivery
---@field status aws.continuum.DeliveryStatus How far delivery to the destination has progressed.
---@field target? aws.continuum.DestinationTarget Where the patch was or will be delivered. Absent while the destination is still being resolved, or when delivery was skipped before a destination was known.
---@field updatedAt string When the delivery status last changed.

---How a patch is encoded, which determines the command that applies it.
---@alias aws.continuum.PatchFormat "GIT_MAILBOX_PATCH"|"GIT_BINARY_DIFF"|"GIT_DIFF"

---Validation's result for one finding within a multi-finding bundle.
---@class aws.continuum.PerFindingResult
---@field findingId aws.continuum.FindingId The finding assessed.
---@field exploitable aws.continuum.ExploitabilityVerdict Exploitability verdict for this finding.
---@field confidence? aws.continuum.ValidationConfidence Confidence in this finding's verdict. Absent when out of range.
---@field flowVerdicts? aws.continuum.FlowVerdicts Per-flow verdicts recorded for this finding.
---@field reasoningChain? aws.continuum.ReasoningSteps Reasoning chain recorded for this finding.
---@field exploitArtifact? aws.continuum.ValidationExploitArtifact Exploit artifact produced for this finding, when there was one.

---@alias aws.continuum.PerFindingResults aws.continuum.PerFindingResult[]

---One producer's conclusion about one subject on one scoring dimension.
---@class aws.continuum.PrevalidationSignal
---@field subjectRef? aws.continuum.ArtifactCitation What this signal is about, such as a finding or issue reference.
---@field dimension? aws.continuum.SignalDimension The axis this signal speaks to. Absent when the producer reported a dimension with no mapping yet.
---@field signalStrength? aws.continuum.SignalStrength The signal's own rating. This is an input to scoring and is NOT the finding's severity.
---@field conclusion? aws.continuum.ArtifactText The producer's conclusion.
---@field producerId? aws.continuum.IssueArtifactProducerName Stable name of the producer that emitted this signal.
---@field producerVersion? aws.continuum.ArtifactCitation Version of that producer.
---@field confidence? aws.continuum.ValidationConfidence The producer's confidence in this conclusion, on its native 0-1 scale. Absent when the stored value falls outside 0-1.
---@field confidenceReasoning? aws.continuum.SignalConfidenceReasoning Why the producer is or is not sure, kept structured rather than prose.
---@field computed? aws.continuum.SignalComputation The deterministic values the producer computed from its assessment.
---@field preconditions? aws.continuum.SignalPreconditions The four exploit preconditions a likelihood signal assessed, each with the basis the producer had for it.
---@field impactDimensions? aws.continuum.SignalImpactDimensions The three impact dimensions an impact signal assessed, each with the basis the producer had for it. These are what the computed impact band is derived from.
---@field exploitability? aws.continuum.SignalExploitability What validation established about exploitability, on an exploitability signal. This summarizes the verdict the signal was derived from; the proof itself is the VALIDATION_EVIDENCE artifact it cites.

---@alias aws.continuum.PrevalidationSignals aws.continuum.PrevalidationSignal[]

---Projected content for an EVIDENCE artifact carrying prioritization's prevalidation signals.
---@class aws.continuum.PrevalidationSignalsBody
---@field producedBy? aws.continuum.IssueArtifactProducerName The agent that produced this signal set.
---@field signals? aws.continuum.PrevalidationSignals The signals backing the Issue's proposed severity.

