---@field factors? aws.continuum.ArtifactCitations The individual factors behind it.

---The scoring axis a signal speaks to.
---@alias aws.continuum.SignalDimension "EXPLOITABILITY"|"BLAST_RADIUS"|"NETWORK_EXPOSURE"|"PRECONDITION"|"CODE_CONTEXT"|"LIKELIHOOD_ASSESSMENT"|"IMPACT_ASSESSMENT"

---What validation established about exploitability, as summarized onto the scoring signal derived from it.
---@class aws.continuum.SignalExploitability
---@field verdict? aws.continuum.ExploitabilityVerdict Validation's verdict. `UNCERTAIN` covers a run that was inconclusive — out of budget, an ambiguous failure, or no decisive layer reached — and is never a refutation.
---@field reachedCrownJewels? boolean Whether validation reached the high-value sink the attack path posited. A Boolean rather than an enum: the sink was either reached or it was not, and how far the walk got when it was not is already carried, with more precision, by `highestLayerReached`. An unknown is the absent member.
---@field highestLayerReached? number The highest impact layer validation reached, 1-5, as a measure of how far the attack path was walked.
---@field confidenceTier? aws.continuum.ValidationConfidenceTier How strong the evidence behind the verdict is.
---@field scriptable? boolean Whether the proven exploit is automatable rather than one-off. A Boolean for the same reason as `SignalPrecondition.value`: validation records a bool, and an unknown is the absent member.
---@field sourceValidationArtifactId? aws.continuum.IssueArtifactId The VALIDATION_EVIDENCE artifact on this same issue holding the proof this verdict summarizes. Fetch it with GetCodeIssueArtifact for the full reasoning chain and exploit artifact.

---The three impact dimensions an impact signal assessed. The computed impact band is derived from attackerGains and blastRadius, then shifted by targetValue.
---@class aws.continuum.SignalImpactDimensions
---@field attackerGains? aws.continuum.SignalAttackerGainsDimension What the attacker gains from exploitation.
---@field blastRadius? aws.continuum.SignalBlastRadiusDimension How far the consequences reach.
---@field targetValue? aws.continuum.SignalTargetValueDimension How valuable the target is, which can shift the band off its base value.

---One assessed precondition with the basis behind it.
---@class aws.continuum.SignalPrecondition
---@field value? boolean The producer's determination. A Boolean rather than an enum, against the Common Terms preference for enums on extensibility grounds. The question each precondition answers is closed — is the code reachable, is configuration required, must a user other than the attacker interact — and the only third state, "not determined", is already expressed by omitting this member, which the projection does...
---@field basis? aws.continuum.SignalBasis Where the producer's determination came from.
---@field reason? aws.continuum.ArtifactText The producer's explanation.
---@field missingInfo? aws.continuum.ArtifactText What the producer could not determine, when anything was missing.

---The four preconditions a likelihood signal assessed.
---@class aws.continuum.SignalPreconditions
---@field reachableFromAttacker? aws.continuum.SignalPrecondition Whether the vulnerable code path is reachable by an attacker.
---@field configurationNeeded? aws.continuum.SignalPrecondition Whether exploitation depends on a non-default configuration.
---@field accessLevel? aws.continuum.SignalAccessPrecondition What level of access exploitation requires.
---@field userInteractionRequired? aws.continuum.SignalPrecondition Whether exploitation requires a user other than the attacker to take part, for example by opening a link or a file (CVSS User Interaction).

---A signal's own rating, an input to scoring rather than a finding severity.
---@alias aws.continuum.SignalStrength "NONE"|"WEAK"|"MODERATE"|"STRONG"

---How valuable the exploited target is.
---@alias aws.continuum.SignalTargetValue "HIGH"|"MEDIUM"|"LOW"

---The assessed target-value dimension with the basis behind it.
---@class aws.continuum.SignalTargetValueDimension
---@field value? aws.continuum.SignalTargetValue How valuable the target is. Absent when the producer reported a value with no mapping yet.
---@field basis? aws.continuum.SignalBasis Where the producer's determination came from.
---@field reason? aws.continuum.ArtifactText The producer's explanation.
---@field missingInfo? aws.continuum.ArtifactText What the producer could not determine, when anything was missing.

